+See v2_process.h, v2_process_boot.h and tests/process-check.inc for implementation and harness checks.
 
-GPI has monotonically allocated 0x60000000|serial handles within a session, 16 DC/PS/bitmap slots each, max dimension 2048 and a 32 MiB raw bitmap budget. Bitmap data is bottom-up with DWORD-aligned rows, palettes stored as 00RRGGBB. Supported depths are 1/4/8/24/32, one plane, uncompressed. Header variants 12 (RGB3), 16 (RGB2) and 64 (RGB2) are marshaled manually; the 16-byte prefix is essential for Sarien. Query header writes exactly the requested supported header size. Set/Query bits validate matching dimensions/depth and guest buffers, copy raw rows/palette, and do not provide arbitrary format conversion.
-
-PS logical palettes support up to 256 colors; CreateLogColorTable handles the tested consecutive RGB/PURE path, and SetColor/SetPel use the PS palette. Indexed color matching may select the first duplicate. Selected bitmaps cannot be deleted or selected into two PSs; destruction deselects and stale handles fail. Persistent window PSs permit Sarien worker blits outside BeginPaint. One cooperative VP plus the guest mutex serializes the tested access.
-
-BitBlt supports SRCCOPY (0xCC), three/four points, ordered positive dimensions and checked source/target ranges. Source pixels are snapshotted into top-down RGB32 to handle overlap. Memory targets use nearest-neighbor sampling and palette matching; window output uses StretchDIBits with negative-height DIB, converting bottom-origin guest Y into native top-origin coordinates. Existing regression fixture verifies quadrant colors/orientation/readback/copy/cleanup.
